{#- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    CN THEME TAPE (#cn-theme-tape / .ctt-*) — china.html.j2, mode == 'stocks'.
    主题周期 — 每个主题在周期中的位置，以及本榜对其成分股的处理。

    WHAT THIS IS.
    Charter: research/CHINA_PROPHET_LOSER_INTELLIGENCE_MASTERPLAN_BY_FABLE.md §5 W-C.
    Data:    engine/cn_theme_tape.py — the whole join is Python; this file lays out a
             finished dict. No membership logic, no counting, no sorting here.

    It closes the operator incident of 2026-08-04: Gold Miners read as the top sector
    on several boards and this page said NOTHING about why it carried no picks. The
    facts were already in nightly artifacts — the basket had turned, its members were
    held out upstream, each for a stated reason. Answering it took a forensic session;
    it should have taken a glance. This panel is the standing fix.

    THE THESIS IS THE LAG: A SECTOR TURNS BEFORE ITS NAMES DO. That is the one idea the
    layout has to carry, and it is why the row set is defined by the CYCLE rather than
    by heat. The US tape (templates/_theme_tape.html.j2, #4488) is the structural model
    — one persistent header, fixed count columns, <details> per theme, colour on a
    single glyph — and none of its copy is reused: it answers "the market is heating
    this, what are the picks doing with it", and this one answers "the sector turned,
    where is everybody".

    IT IS AN ACCOUNTING, NOT A LEADERBOARD. Every member of a shown theme lands in
    exactly one column, so a row adds up to the basket's whole membership, and a theme
    with zero picks still gets a row that says so. A panel that only spoke when it had
    a pick would reproduce the silence it exists to fix.

    DESIGN NOTES.
    · THE CYCLE RAIL is the one new object and the panel's signature: five segments in
      cycle order (bottoming → early turn → running → late → rolling over) with one
      marked. It is a POSITION encoding, never a magnitude bar — the vetoed ftr-tape
      idiom (#2232) is exactly a fake magnitude bar, and this is the sanctioned
      opposite: the doctrine's canonised "non-verbal encodings that need no vocabulary
      at all" (§7). It earns its place by making the column SCANNABLE — "which themes
      are early?" answers without reading a word — which a bare phrase cannot do.
      It takes NO hue, on purpose. The cycle read is context with no measured edge
      behind it; colouring it would paint the least-proven thing on the panel as the
      loudest, which is the construction the 2026-07-23 ruling removed.
    · COLOUR APPEARS ON EXACTLY ONE GLYPH — a non-zero `live` count, via --ink-up,
      which flips under 红涨绿跌 at paint. The states are carried by POSITION and by
      the header's words, never by hue. This holds even though the panel's own subject
      is a row with NO live names: hue means "there is something to do today", and an
      early turn that nothing has confirmed is precisely not that. The early-turn story
      is carried by the rail and by the stance sentence instead.
    · A ZERO PRINTS AS AN EN-DASH in its slot rather than collapsing. Printed absence
      is the point of this panel, and a missing cell would break the column scan.
    · The quiet remainder is a FRACTION ("4/6"), never a bare count — the denominator
      is what makes it information instead of decoration (Law 3).
    · Zero animation, zero transition, and no `transform` anywhere. So there is no
      reduced-motion block to gate, and nothing here can trap the Lens popover in a
      containing block. Add either and you must handle both.

    WHERE IT SITS. Directly BELOW the board, mirroring the US panel's placement after
    the operator's 2026-08-04 order ("it's obstructing this entire page"). Context that
    changes no decision reads AFTER the decision it contextualises. It is also the
    honest reading order here: you look at the picks, then ask what happened to
    everything else — which is the question this panel answers.

    TIERS (docs/DESIGN_DOCTRINE.md):
      1 GLANCE  eyebrow · one grid line per theme · a stance sentence · one footer line
      2 HOVER   the panel `?` carries the method AND the Law-5 null receipt; per-theme
                receipts (cycle position, turn strength) ride data-tip-*
      3 STUDY   the expanded member lists, the per-name reasons, the theme vehicle,
                and china_sector_desk.html for every theme
    Every stance sentence is chosen MECHANICALLY from the counts by
    engine/cn_theme_tape.py `_stance_for` — no free-form text reaches this file, and
    the verbs come from the doctrine's sanctioned stance vocabulary.
    No translated text ever enters a title= attribute (CI-guarded); every tip is a
    hand-written data-tip-* pair, never piped through t()/help(), which emit spans and
    would break attribute quoting.

    GATING. china_stocks.html is edge-gated by OMISSION: it is absent from the Caddy
    public allow-list, so an anonymous visitor is redirected by app/regwall.py before
    any HTML is served, and every signed-in visitor — free or paid — gets the board in
    full with no client-side tier markup anywhere on the page. So this panel adds no
    gate of its own: it would be theatre to collapse names here that the board prints
    in full a few hundred pixels above, for the same visitor. `.ctt-names` is
    nonetheless the member-roster hook, mirroring the US `.tt-names`, so if this page
    ever joins the public list the collapse is one selector in tier_preview.js — and
    tests/test_cn_theme_tape.py pins the class so that stays true.

    CONTEXT IT READS (fail-open; absence renders exactly like a quiet tape):
      cn_theme_tape  {as_of, board_as_of, rows[], n_themes, overflow, flow_live, ...}
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -#}

{%- macro ct_t(en, zh='') -%}
